bitors:** Cyanide (blocks ETC), ATP synthase inhibitors (like oligomycin), and uncouplers (like DNP) disrupt ATP production.\n  - **Activators:** ADP and AMP stimulate glycolysis and the ETC by promoting ATP demand.\n\n- **Environmental Effects:**\n  - Oxygen availability determines whether aerobic respiration, anaerobic respiration, or fermentation occurs.\n  - Temperature and pH can influence enzyme activity and ATP yield.",
